        "comments": "URL -- http://www.jgi.doe.gov/chlamy\nJGI Project ID: 2662209\nStock culture is available from www.chlamy.org\nContacts: Daniel Rokhsar (DSRokhsar@lbl.gov)\nArthur Grossman (arthurg@stanford.edu)\nThis assembly, v3.0, was constructed with JAZZ, the JGI assembler, from WGS reads including small insert plasmids, fosmids and BACs. After trimming for vector and quality, 2.1 Million paired end sequencing reads assembled into 1557 scaffolds totaling 120 Mbp. Roughly half of the genome is contained in 24 scaffolds all at least 1.6 Mb in length. The depth of sequence coverage for the main genome scaffolds is estimated at approximately 12.8x.\nAnnotation done by JGI-PGF and Chlamydomonas Annotation Team\nThe JGI and collaborators endorse the principles for the distribution and use of large scale sequencing data adopted by the larger genome sequencing community and urge users of this data to follow them. It is our intention to publish the work of this project in a timely fashion and we welcome collaborative interaction on the project and analysis.\n(http://www.genome.gov/page.cfm?pageID=10506376)\nABCN01011186 and DS497466 were suppressed because they may contain contamination.",
